 ers\, interpreters and assemblers
DESCRIPTION:IEB Grade 11 - Pascal - Access - Public school (DBE\, four term
 s) - T1 W9\n\nProgramming:\n- Pascal 16 (part): Smart data - Classes and ob
 jects\n    focus: classes: fields and methods\, private/protected/public\, 
 default and parameterised constructors\, accessor\, mutator and toString\, 
 encapsulation and information hiding\, overloading\, private helper methods
 \, static vs instance\, constant fields\, class diagrams\; parameters into 
 the methods of an object\, return types\, a string with fields separated by
  #\, and the scope and lifetime of variables\, fields and parameters\; arra
 ys of objects\, compared with parallel arrays\; abstraction: designing clas
 ses to encapsulate fields and methods\, with the object as a backend separa
 te from the user interface\; decomposition: finding classes\, fields and me
 thods with noun-verb analysis of a user story\n    https://itcoder.co.za/le
 sson.php?c=pascal&id=lesson16\n\nTheory:\n- Compilers\, interpreters and as
 semblers\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=theory11&id=translators\n-
  Numbers in a fixed number of bits\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=
 theory11&id=fixedbits
